Log in to MangaDex and save the login for follows


mangadex-dl login [OPTIONS]


OPTIONS:
  -h, --help                        Print this help message and exit
      --credentials FILE            Read login details from FILE
      --password-stdin              Read the password from stdin
      --no-input                    Never prompt; fail if a login is needed
      --version                     Print the version and exit
      --json                        Write machine-readable JSON to stdout
  -q, --quiet                       Only print errors
  -v, --verbose                     Print more detail to stderr (repeatable)
      --color WORD [auto]           Color stderr: auto, always or never

Logs in to MangaDex with your password and saves the login (never the
password) for 'mangadex-dl follows', readable only by you, in
$XDG_STATE_HOME/mangadex-dl/session.json (~/.local/state/mangadex-dl/ by
default). It always logs in afresh, so it also renews a login that ended.

Logging in needs a MangaDex personal API client: create one at
https://mangadex.org/settings (API Clients); a new client may need approval
by MangaDex staff before it works. In a terminal, login asks for what it
does not know yet: the client id and secret, your username and your
password. The client and the username of the saved login are reused, so
usually only the password is asked.

The details can also come from a private file (chmod 600):
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mangadex-dl/credentials (~/.config/mangadex-dl/ by
default) or --credentials FILE, one 'key = value' per line with the keys
client_id, client_secret, username and, optionally, password.
Never put a password on the command line.

To switch accounts, run 'mangadex-dl logout' first, or use --credentials
with the other account.

Nothing is written to stdout, also with --json.

Examples:
  Log in, typing the details at the prompts:
    mangadex-dl login
  In a script, with the password from a password manager:
    pass show mangadex | mangadex-dl login --password-stdin

Exit status:
  0   success
  1   runtime failure (including a failed write to stdout)
  2   usage error
  3   network or API failure (connection, TLS, timeout, server error)
  4   title or list not found on MangaDex (a private list counts)
  5   no downloadable chapters matched the language and selection
  6   incomplete: at least one output file failed
  7   several titles failed in different ways (see per-title results)
  8   follows/login: not logged in, or the saved login expired
  9   follows/login: MangaDex rejected the login details
  70  internal error (a bug: please report it)
